  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Alan Jope  (born 1964) is a British businessman. He was Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of Unilever from January 2019 until June 2023, succeeding Paul Polman. Upon stepping down as CEO of Unilever, Jope was succeeded by Hein Schumacher who took on the role from July 2023.\nIn the 2024 Birthday Honours, Jope was appointed a Commander of the Order of the British Empire (CBE) for services to business.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
